+# REPORT 08 — Status DONE
+
+Python-agent recipe, "Gate a retry-policy change in ten minutes". Coder: Claude Opus 5.5 (high), worktree `wt-recipes` (branch sprint/recipes at fcd79ce). No git state changed; nothing under `src/arci/**` or any frozen file touched.
+
+## Changes
+- `examples/recipes/python_agent/`: `app/__init__.py`, `app/v1.py` (`run(task, tools, rng)`: confirm; if the order is not held, `reserve` with up to 3 attempts, then confirm), `app/v2.py` (the same without the retry loop), `tests/__init__.py`, `tests/world.py` (51 lines, fully typed: tools `reserve` and `confirm`; per seed, 75% of orders start held and 20% of reserve backends time out twice; `passed` = the task's order is confirmed in the final state), `arci.yaml` (generated by the exact `arci init` command below; the test regenerates it and compares bytes), `README.md` (108 lines).
+- `docs/recipes/python-agent.md` (132 lines): the narrative; one `<<recorded run>>` placeholder for the orchestrator (smoke run + confirmatory run + wall times).
+- `tests/unit/recipes/__init__.py`, `tests/unit/recipes/test_python_agent.py` (5 tests).
+- Design of the world: v2 survives the injected `tool_timeout:reserve:0` only when the order arrived held (it never calls `reserve` then), so the candidate drops without collapsing; v1 fails only when it must reserve on a twice-failing backend (0.25 x 0.20 = 0.05). Expected rates 0.95 / 0.75 match the README's `arci plan` command. Not a copy of `arci.demo.world` (two tools, no stock, no confirm outage).
+
+## Tests
+- `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/recipes -q` -> `9 passed in 28.45s` (5 of them T08). Slowest: `test_plan_then_the_confirmatory_descriptor` 17.8 s (`arci plan` exact enumeration to N=400); the module fixture (init + run) about 2.5 s.
+- `.venv/bin/ruff format --check .` -> `315 files already formatted`; `.venv/bin/ruff check .` -> `All checks passed!`; `.venv/bin/basedpyright` -> `0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 notes`; `shasum -a 256 -c FROZEN.sha256 | grep -v OK` -> nothing.
+- Also green: `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/recipes tests/unit/docs tests/unit/init -q`.
+- Real end-to-end from a tmp copy (console script `.venv/bin/arci`, PYTHONPATH unset, committed `arci.yaml` removed):
+  - `arci init checkout-retry --baseline app.v1:run --candidate app.v2:run --toolset tests.world:make_world --oracle tests.world:passed --task '{"order_id": "order-7"}' --fault tool_timeout:reserve:0` -> exit 0, stdout `arci run arci.yaml`, stderr empty; `cmp` with the committed `arci.yaml`: identical.
+  - `arci run arci.yaml` -> exit 2, last stdout `VERDICT: INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2)`, baseline 8/8, candidate 2/8, wall 1.7 s; stderr = the SMOKE DESIGN line and `INCONCLUSIVE at n_per_arm=8 is the expected smoke result; choose a confirmatory N with arci plan before re-running.`
+  - `arci plan --baseline-rate 0.95 --candidate-rate 0.75 --target-verdict BLOCK` -> smallest tested N meeting P(BLOCK) >= 0.8: 400.
+  - Confirmatory (init `checkout-retry-n400 ... --n 400 --out confirm.yaml` + `base_seed: 1000`, `prior_runs: ["checkout-retry"]`): `arci run confirm.yaml` -> `VERDICT: BLOCK (exit 1)`, baseline 390/400, candidate 296/400, bounds [-0.3018, -0.1633], wall 1:29.5 on this machine (coder's run; not pasted into the docs, which cite only the orchestrator's recorded run).
+  - diff / minimize / bundle / replay on `faults:00000:candidate`: all exit 0; replay `REPRODUCED` (also from a different directory, without the checkout).
+
+## Deviations
+- The test runs `arci run arci.yaml` exactly as the README writes it (the memo's command), not `... --workers 4`: `--workers` defaults to 4 (`src/arci/cli.py`, `run` parser), so it is the same run, and (c) requires the README's commands to be the ones the test runs.
+- The README adds a setup line (`cp -R examples/recipes/python_agent checkout && cd checkout && rm arci.yaml`): the committed `arci.yaml` is exactly what `arci init` writes, and init refuses an existing file without `--force`, so running the memo command in an unmodified tree would exit 3. The test emulates those three commands (copytree, cwd, unlink) and asserts they are the README's first three.
+- Test (c) is stronger than asked: it pins the full ordered list of README bash commands, runs every `arci` command except `arci run confirm.yaml` (800 trials, about 90 s; the confirm descriptor is still written by the README's command, extended with the README's yaml block, and compiled/seal-checked), and skips `uv tool install` (network).
+- The confirmatory run uses a new experiment id with `base_seed: 1000` and `prior_runs` added by hand (README yaml block), so its seeds are disjoint from the smoke run's and the report lists the smoke run; init has no flags for either.
+
+## Open issues
+- `uv tool install agent-reliability-ci` in the README only works after the PyPI release; the README says to use the clone's environment until then.
+- `test_plan_then_the_confirmatory_descriptor` spends ~18 s in `arci plan`; under 60 s here, but the slowest recipe test on a slow CI runner.
